  "id": "reasoned-action-model",
  "term": "reasoned action model",
  "definition": "The reasoned action model is a framework for explaining behavior in which a person’s attitudes toward a behavior and the subjective norms they perceive shape their intention to act, and that intention then influences the behavior itself.",
